oolu_0145hEwK1oviT36qDRRdW45m":{"command":"V=/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library; L=/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library; for b in framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology claim--differential-tissue-adaptation-rates principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue; do f=$(find $V $L -name \"$b.md\" | head -1); echo \"## $f\"; grep -m1 '^chapter' \"$f\"; grep -o -i 'quasi-isometric[^.]*' \"$f\" | head -2; done; ls $V/strength-and-conditioning/science-and-practice-of-strength-training--zatsiorsky/ 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'joint-strength-curves|accommodation-and-the'; grep -n -i 'minimal significance' /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--three-bodybuilding-regimes-and-add-on-methods.md | head -2","description":"Check linked entries' chapters and content"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffrjm8FN6R2Ckmfc7MuU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0488446a-e67c-4731-9124-48f36a177ed3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:30:20.060Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"0488446a-e67c-4731-9124-48f36a177ed3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ef194c20-d5f8-4d01-bce0-254fc908bea5","agentId":"aa8a0297ea9df7045","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0145hEwK1oviT36qDRRdW45m","type":"tool_result","content":"## /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology.md\nchapter: \"1.8-1.11\"\nQuasi-isometric\" action is defined separately: the slow, near-static muscle\nquasi-isometric,\" a\n## /Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--differential-tissue-adaptation-rates.md\nchapter: \"1.6\"\n## /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue.md\nchapter: \"6.9.4\"\nframework--joint-strength-curves-sticking-points-and-moment-arm.md\nprinciple--accommodation-and-the-diminishing-returns-law.md\n39:**When NOT to apply** — Not as sport strength methods. The authors say bodybuilding methods \"are of minimal significance for developing most of the specific functional types of strength fitness required in competitive sport\" (PDF p. 412 / printed p. 401). Supersets are, in the authors' words, \"not intended to develop strength\" (PDF p. 408). Eric's baseline (line 104): \"single-joint assistance work is kept to a small share of total volume\" **Inferred (transcript + slides)**. Inference: pre-exhaustion and isolation-led splits build a session around single-joint work, which runs against that rule outside a dedicated hypertrophy block. Eric's baseline (line 61): \"No sport performs true 1RM testing.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q10)**; the regimes' percentages would rest on projected maxes.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"011c5774-3801-4c78-840e-7b2cada9181c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:30:20.525Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology.md\nchapter: \"1.8-1.11\"\nQuasi-isometric\" action is defined separately: the slow, near-static muscle\nquasi-isometric,\" a\n## /Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--differential-tissue-adaptation-rates.md\nchapter: \"1.6\"\n## /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue.md\nchapter: \"6.9.4\"\nframework--joint-strength-curves-sticking-points-and-moment-arm.md\nprinciple--accommodation-and-the-diminishing-returns-law.md\n39:**When NOT to apply** — Not as sport strength methods. The authors say bodybuilding methods \"are of minimal significance for developing most of the specific functional types of strength fitness required in competitive sport\" (PDF p. 412 / printed p. 401). Supersets are, in the authors' words, \"not intended to develop strength\" (PDF p. 408). Eric's baseline (line 104): \"single-joint assistance work is kept to a small share of total volume\" **Inferred (transcript + slides)**. Inference: pre-exhaustion and isolation-led splits build a session around single-joint work, which runs against that rule outside a dedicated hypertrophy block. Eric's baseline (line 61): \"No sport performs true 1RM testing.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q10)**; the regimes' percentages would rest on projected maxes.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0488446a-e67c-4731-9124-48f36a177ed3","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
