he \"minimal significance\" sentence. PDF 405-410 were checked on the text layer, with round 1's page images as backup. Every fixed sentence in the 8 edited files was read in full against the page, not against the fix log."," "," ## Targeted checks"," "]},{"oldStart":18,"oldLines":7,"newStart":18,"newLines":7,"lines":[" |---|---|---|---|"," | framework--strength-training-aims-and-method-chart-figs-7-1-and-7-2.md | **GO** | None found. | checked: the five sources and \"Only in recent years, has science begun to investigate seriously ...\" at PDF 404 / printed 393; superslow, active stretching, connective tissue and cyclical-activity quotes at PDF 405 / printed 394, each word for word; \"rapid reference for the major methods which are most frequently used in the training of high-level athletes\" and the magazine-methods exclusion at PDF 414 / printed 403; the closing Inference is labelled; new links resolve and their stated chapters match (`framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology` is Ch 1.8-1.11 and defines quasi-isometric; `claim--differential-tissue-adaptation-rates` is Ch 1.6; `principle--loading-volume-...` is Ch 6.9.4); new When NOT line matches PDF 404. Fig 7.1/7.2 content was GO in round 1 and is unchanged. `untested` fits the rule (taxonomy with one unevidenced ordering). |"," | framework--maximal-supramaximal-circa-maximal-and-submaximal-methods.md | **GO** | Fix 1 landed in all three parts. | checked: scope sentence opens \"Why `contested`\"; \"As worded, both sentences describe\"; \"optimal recovery intervals between sets\" at PDF 406 / printed 395 (the page says \"This 1RM set with optimal recovery intervals between sets\", a fair reading); the PDF 409 sentence does open the interval section that runs into Cluster Training (10-20 s \"in an extended set\"); When NOT now names injury warnings for eccentrics (\"carries an increased risk of injury\") and cheating (\"if injury is to be avoided\") only, with no warning for forced reps, matching PDF 407. The consistency edit (\"two values that may describe different methods\") matches the scoped reason. `contested` scoped to one rest figure is consistent with the rule. |","-| framework--three-bodybuilding-regimes-and-add-on-methods.md | **FIX** (minor) | Fix 2 landed (`supported`; \"Inference: split routines and zone training ...\"). New inconsistency exposed by the confidence change: When NOT opens \"Not as sport strength methods. The authors say bodybuilding methods 'are of minimal significance ...' (PDF p. 412)\". On PDF 412 that sentence refers to \"a host of different bodybuilding methods\" introduced under Miscellaneous Methods (\"These are not discussed at length here because they are of minimal significance\"), not to the three regimes on PDF 408. The fix log uses that same quote to keep the miscellaneous entry `untested` while this entry goes to `supported`, so the quote cannot belong to both. The PDF 405 rule also says that if the strength deficit is small \"submaximal bodybuilding methods should be relied upon\" for athletes, so \"Not as sport strength methods\" overstates. | Replace the first two sentences of When NOT with: \"Not as the main method for speed-strength or explosive qualities: the authors send athletes with a large strength deficit to weightlifting and reactive methods, and keep submaximal bodybuilding methods for a small deficit (PDF p. 405 / printed p. 394).\" Keep the supersets sentence and the rest unchanged. |","+| framework--three-bodybuilding-regimes-and-add-on-methods.md | **FIX** (minor) | Fix 2 landed (`supported`; \"Inference: split routines and zone training ...\"). New inconsistency exposed by the confidence change: When NOT opens \"Not as sport strength methods. The authors say bodybuilding methods 'are of minimal significance ...' (PDF p. 412)\". On PDF 412 that sentence refers to \"a host of different bodybuilding methods\" introduced under Miscellaneous Methods (\"These are not discussed at length here because they are of minimal significance\"), not to the three regimes on PDF 408. The fix log uses that same quote to keep the miscellaneous entry `untested` while this entry goes to `supported`, so the quote cannot belong to both. The PDF 405 rule also says that if the strength deficit is small \"submaximal bodybuilding methods should be relied upon\" for athletes, so \"Not as sport strength methods\" overstates. | Replace the first two sentences of When NOT with: \"Not when the strength deficit is large: the authors then concentrate on weightlifting and reactive methods, and keep submaximal bodybuilding methods for a small deficit (PDF p. 405 / printed p. 394).\" Keep the supersets sentence and the rest unchanged. |"," | framework--set-structures-plateau-step-stripping-and-pyramids.md | **GO** | Fix 3 landed. | checked: `supported`; \"Inference: step sets can find a working load ...\"; \"Plateau sets are for novices and transition phases (PDF p. 408). Inference: not for a peaking block.\" Plateau \"commonly used during the early stages of training novices or for transitional active rest phases\", stripping \"commonly used for muscle endurance and definition training\" (PDF 408 / printed 397), pyramid values and \"rarely used by serious athletes today\" (PDF 409 / printed 398), item 7 (PDF 413 / printed 402). Keeping the \"rarely used\" caveat alongside `supported` is coherent: the structures are established; the caveat is the authors' preference among them. |"," | framework--interval-resistance-training-and-cluster-sets.md | **FIX** (minor) | Fix 4 landed: the direct same-paragraph statements (5RM minimum, 4-6RM, 10-20% strip, 75-90%) lead \"Why `contested`\" and the When NOT list, all matching PDF 409-410 / printed 398-399. Two problems remain. (1) \"both of which take the load below that minimum\" is true of the 6RM end and the 10-20% strip, not of the 4RM-5RM end of \"4-6RM\"; the fix log claims a narrowing that the sentence does not carry. (2) Consistency with the scoped `contested` reasons in the maximal and contrast entries: this entry's reason never says the extensive and intensive interval prescriptions (30-40% / 5-6 x 20-30 / 1-2 min; 50-60% / 3-6 sets to failure / 10-90 s) are not in dispute, so a reader filtering by confidence would read them as contested. | (1) Change \"both of which take the load below that minimum\" to \"both of which can take the load below that minimum\". (2) Open \"Why `contested`\" with: \"The rating applies only to the cluster-set loads; the extensive and intensive interval prescriptions are not in dispute.\" |"," | framework--hybrid-repetitions-and-hybrid-sets.md | **GO** | Fix 5 landed. | checked: the superscript paragraph against the PDF 336 image and the PDF 411 crop (see Targeted checks); \"When a circuit is to be condensed into one station (the authors' use, PDF p. 410)\" matches \"Instead of doing three separate exercises at three different stations, one can do all of them in a single repetition or at a single station\"; the time/space clause is now labelled Inference; Example reads \"written 80³ (three sets by the 6.6.2 convention)\". `untested` fits the rule: examples \"may be devised by the inventive coach\" (PDF 411), no load or rest parameters. |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7a_opus_round2.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08629840-af06-4e09-8f3e-dd5bbff4710e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
