{"parentUuid":"23723d76-93f6-4861-858c-cff9b52feb50","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa8a0297ea9df7045","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffrwT7MupeSPgQBQFi91","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":798,"cache_read_input_tokens":167617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":798,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6567,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffrwCr7W9bBktSSjaViJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6919f216-7eda-4e88-8aba-59230263ba16","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:33:00.555Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"6919f216-7eda-4e88-8aba-59230263ba16","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aa8a0297ea9df7045","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffrwT7MupeSPgQBQFi91","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** 7 GO, 3 FIX, 0 NO-GO.\n\nAll seven round-1 fixes are in the files and match the pages. None of them introduced a new factual error. The fixer's three disagreements with round 1 hold up:\n- **Contrast entry:** it correctly keeps Murray (1959) and Van Huss (1962), the two Western studies on PDF 175 that found an effect. Round 1's proposed wording would have dropped them.\n- **Hybrid entry:** citing the notation convention to PDF 335-336, not 336 alone, is right.\n- **Interval entry:** the 6RM-vs-5RM point was meant to be narrowed. The arithmetic is right, but the sentence still says too much (fix 2 below).\n\n**Targeted checks:**\n- **Superscript notation:** confirmed on the PDF 336 image. \"10(60)¹, 8(70)¹, 6(80)²\" is the same work as the 60 x 10, 70 x 8, 80 x 6, 80 x 6 list at the foot of PDF 335, so the superscript is the number of sets. The PDF 411 image shows 80³ over 3+5+2, so the entry's \"three sets\" reading is right.\n- **PDF 175 quotes:** the Western and Russian quotes in the contrast entry match the page image word for word, citation lists included.\n- **Confidence:** the rule is applied consistently across all 10. The two upgrades to `supported` (three regimes, set structures) fit the page. The eight unchanged ratings fit the rule, though segmental is borderline: it has parameters but no load or rest.\n- **Mechanical:** every file has the six headers. No em dashes outside headers, no wrapped links, no review-history wording. All 45 wikilinks resolve in staging or the vault.\n\n**The three fixes** are wording edits only; no page needs re-checking:\n1. **Three bodybuilding regimes, When NOT to apply.** It cites the PDF 412 \"of minimal significance\" sentence as if it covered the regimes. The page image shows that sentence opens the Miscellaneous Methods section. The fix log also uses that same sentence to keep the miscellaneous entry `untested`, so it can't support both. PDF 405 also says to rely on submaximal bodybuilding methods when the strength deficit is small, so \"Not as sport strength methods\" goes too far. Replace the opening with: \"Not when the strength deficit is large: the authors then concentrate on weightlifting and reactive methods, and keep submaximal bodybuilding methods for a small deficit (PDF p. 405 / printed p. 394).\"\n2. **Interval and cluster sets.**\n   - Change \"both of which take the load below that minimum\" to \"both of which can take the load below that minimum\". Only the 6RM end of \"4-6RM\" is below a 5RM.\n   - Open \"Why `contested`\" with: \"The rating applies only to the cluster-set loads; the extensive and intensive interval prescriptions are not in dispute.\" This matches how the maximal and contrast entries scope their ratings.\n3. **Sticking points, When to apply.** \"stalled for weeks\", \"a lifter with a training history\" and \"pick one or two changes at a time\" are the writer's, not the authors'. Rewrite as: \"When a lift has reached a sticking point, as a repertoire to choose from (PDF p. 413). Inference: change one or two things at a time, in a lifter with a training history, so the cause of any change can be seen.\"\n\nThe chart entry and the two spot-checked entries (miscellaneous variations, sticking points) were checked against the PDF 404 and 412-414 page images. PDF 405-410 were checked against the PDF's text, with round 1's page images as backup. No new missing ideas; the five from round 1 are now in the chart entry and quoted correctly.\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7a_opus_round2.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":798,"cache_read_input_tokens":167617,"output_tokens":1362,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":798},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1362,"cache_read_input_tokens":167617,"cache_creation_input_tokens":798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":798,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffrwCr7W9bBktSSjaViJ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"971c5c8e-e1fc-46d1-ae1b-715e5bd75e7b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:33:04.572Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
